        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Budget for the installation as seriously as for the generator, because on many properties it costs as much or more. The variable that moves it most is distance — a unit sited near both the gas meter and the electrical panel is a straightforward job, while one sixty feet away across a driveway means trenching, long gas piping and heavy cable.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Two things are worth settling before you take quotes. Have the electrical panel assessed, because an upgrade is the item most likely to turn a predictable price into a surprise. And have the gas meter capacity confirmed, because a meter sized for a furnace and water heater may not support a standby generator, and upsizing is a separate utility job.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then compare line items rather than totals, and question whole-house capacity if it is the default offer. Selected circuits with load shedding, and a soft starter on the air conditioning condenser, can together move you down a generator size and save considerably more than either measure costs.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            One scheduling note worth acting on: order in a quiet period rather than during a storm. Demand for both units and installers spikes immediately after every significant regional outage, and households that decide during one frequently wait months rather than weeks.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Finally, budget for the years after the install as well as the install itself — annual servicing, a starting battery every few years, and the small weekly fuel cost of the self-test. A standby generator that has not been serviced is the one that fails on the night you need it.
          </p>
